[3] TCP/IP Model: (Transmission Control Protocol/ Internet Protocol)
TCP is a reliable transmission as if any packages is failed to deliver then it resends the certain package.

1) Application layer: 
* The application layer is the combination of application, presentation and session layer of the OSI model.

2) Transport layer:
* The transport layer determines the protocol used as in OSI model.

3) Internet layer:
* The internet layer is same as the network layer. 
* It is responsible for routing, logical addressing, packetization and fragmentation.

4) Network Interface layer:
* The network interface layer is combination of both data link layer and physical layer.
* It controls MAC addressing to specific NIC(Network Interface Card) , Physical transmission and Error detection.

5) Three-Way Handsake:
* TCP is a connection based protocol in which the sender sends an syncronize bit(SYN) to the receiver. It requests the receiver for connection.
* The receiver sends SYN/ACK bit to sender when its accepts the connection request. It also contains the SYN bit by the sender.
* Then the sender sends an acknowledgement bit(ACK) to the receiver.
* After the three way handsake the data is sent safely between the connected devices.

[4] DNS(Domain Name System):
DNS maps the domain name with its server IP.

1) First looks for local DNS cache or "hosts file".

2) If not found requests recursive DNS server. The details of the recursive DNS server is located at the router or the computer. This server contains results of popular domains.

3) If no results found it passes request to root name server.

4) Then the root name server redirects the request to Top Level Domain(TLD) server.

5) The TLD server pass down the request to the Authoritative Name Server. Each domains are stored in the Authoritative Name Server somewhere.

[5] Commands:

1) ping command:
* ping is a command which is used to check whether a connection to remote computer is possible or not.
* Syntax: ping <target> [options]

2) traceroute command:
* It is used to trace the packets to the destination whatever route does the packets take to reach the destination. 
* It utilizes ICMP(Internet Control Message Protocol) used to report connection issues and transmission errors.
* Syntax: traceroute <destination> [options]

3) whois lookup:
* It is used to find information about the domain registration.
* Syntax: whois <domain>

4) dig command:
* It is used to retrieve information from the name server.
* Syntax: dig <domain> @<dns-server-ip>
